From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 12:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: flush PPE consumer during stop

The PPE core quiesces normal producer notifications before it drains the
REO2PPE completion ring.  Completion callbacks from that final drain still
return RX buffers to ath12k, so advance the WLAN consumer to the matching
EDMA position even while the rest of direct switching is quiesced.  This
keeps both owners synchronized across the next start and avoids replaying
already-completed descriptors after recovery.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
@@ -383,7 +383,7 @@ static void ath12k_ppe_ds_reo_cons_updat
 	struct hal_srng *srng;
 	u16 cons;
 
-	if (!ppe->node || READ_ONCE(ppe->quiesced))
+	if (!ppe->node)
 		return;
 
 	cons = qcom_ppe_ds_reo2ppe_cons(ppe->node);
-- 
